     "cell_layout": "One value per cell of the FULL InMAP grid, laid out LAYER-MAJOR over the model's 27 layers: 8 ground-grid layers of 52411 cells each, then 19 coarse layers of 9324, and 8*52411 + 19*9324 = 596444 = N_ALL. Model layers 0..7 share a byte-identical horizontal grid, so the cell directly above source cell `c` in layer `l` is the flat index `l*N_SRC + c` — which is how the plume-rise observeds read the meteorology at a stack's own layer without any 2-D view.",
     "note": "`format` and the pinned .zarray params are not expressible in the 0.8.0 source schema (G1); the runner sets format at provider creation. Everything here is a single-chunk 1-D array (~4.8 MB each) read in full — value invention's rectangle filter reads the whole grid, and the meteorology gather reaches any of the 27 layers. The SOURCE-cell prefix [0:N_SRC] of W/S/E/N is DECLARED as the src_W/src_S/src_E/src_N variables' `select` range rather than sliced by the caller (esm-spec 8.9.2). This loader has NO gated_select: nothing here is big enough to gate, and keeping it off the SR loaders is what lets each of those gate its own emission layer."
    }
   }
