  "ISRM_SR_L0": {
   "kind": "static",
   "source": {
    "url_template": "s3://inmap-model/isrm_v1.2.2.zarr/"
   },
   "reference": {
    "url": "https://inmap.run/blog/2022/12/15/tutorial/",
    "notes": "InMAP ISRM v1.2.1 zarr store on the inmap-model S3 bucket, emission layer 0."
   },
   "metadata": {
    "esio_format": "zarr",
    "tags": [
     "isrm",
     "source_receptor",
     "air_quality",
     "zarr",
     "emis_layer_0"
    ],
    "x_esd": {
     "format": "zarr",
     "zarr_format": 2,
     "consolidated": false,
     "sr_dim_order": [
      "emisLayer",
      "source",
      "receptor"
     ],
     "arrays": {
      "SOA": {
       "shape": [
        3,
        52411,
        52411
       ],
       "chunks": [
        1,
        5,
        52411
       ],
       "dtype": "<f4",
       "compressor": "blosc:lz4:clevel5:shuffle1",
       "fill": 0.0,
       "order": "C"
      },
      "pNO3": {
       "shape": [
        3,
        52411,
        52411
       ],
       "chunks": [
        1,
        5,
        52411
       ],
       "dtype": "<f4"
      },
      "pNH4": {
       "shape": [
        3,
        52411,
        52411
       ],
       "chunks": [
        1,
        5,
        52411
       ],
       "dtype": "<f4"
      },
      "pSO4": {
       "shape": [
        3,
        52411,
        52411
       ],
       "chunks": [
        1,
        5,
        52411
       ],
       "dtype": "<f4"
      },
      "PrimaryPM25": {
       "shape": [
        3,
        52411,
        52411
       ],
       "chunks": [
        1,
        5,
        52411
       ],
       "dtype": "<f4"
      }
     },
     "gated_select": {
      "axes": [
       {
        "fixed": [
         0
        ]
       },
       {
        "gated_by": "emis_src_cells"
       },
       "all"
      ],
      "applies_to": [
       "SOA",
       "pNO3",
       "pNH4",
       "pSO4",
       "PrimaryPM25"
      ]
     },
     "note": "Per-axis selection over the native SR dims [emisLayer, source, receptor] = [3, 52411, 52411]. `{\"fixed\":[0]}` takes emission layer 0 and DROPS the axis; `{\"gated_by\":\"emis_src_cells\"}` takes the DERIVED support set the pushdown rewrite invents, in its canonical member order; `\"all\"` keeps the receptor axis. The three sibling loaders ISRM_SR_L0/L1/L2 differ in NOTHING but that fixed index, which is what makes each SR model parameter rank-2 [src_cells, rcv_cells] with the gated axis at non-fixed position 0 — the shape the rewrite's detector and the gate consumer both require. A single rank-3 SR array would satisfy neither. The engine defers this provider until value invention has materialised the gating set, then delivers each `applies_to` array pre-sliced to the compact [emis_src_cells, rcv_cells] slab, so none of the ~330 GB matrix is folded (G2)."
    }
   }
  },
  "Emis": {
   "kind": "static",
   "source": {
    "url_template": "REPLACED-BY-THE-CALLER"
   },
   "reference": {
    "notes": "The caller's own point emissions, written out of a GeoDataFrame as a zipped shapefile set and uploaded as an EarthSciLab dataset. The url is a placeholder: a dispatched run reads the document's own loaders, so the caller rewrites this with the dataset's store url before it sends the document. There is no upstream copy to point at, because the layer is the caller's."
   },
   "metadata": {
    "esio_format": "shapefile",
    "tags": [
     "shapefile",
     "point",
     "emissions",
     "user_supplied"
    ],
    "x_esd": {
     "format": "shapefile",
     "container": "zip",
     "crs": "EPSG:4269",
     "note": "The reader is READER-ONLY: it decodes rings and .dbf columns and declares the file's CRS, and it reprojects nothing. `member` names the .shp inside the zip (the .dbf/.shx/.prj sidecars are the same stem) and never enters the cache key. `nvert_max` is the DECLARED vertex-axis width: every part is right-padded to it by repeating its final vertex, and the reader raises rather than silently widening, so the caller computes it from the frame it is about to write. One row per shapefile PART, with the record's .dbf attributes replicated.",
     "columns": {
      "PM25": "kg/yr",
      "VOC": "kg/yr",
      "NOx": "kg/yr",
      "NH3": "kg/yr",
      "SOx": "kg/yr"
     }
    }
   },
   "reader_options": {
    "member": "emis.shp",
    "nvert_max": 1
   },
   "extent": {
    "metaparameter": "N_REC"
   }
  }
 },
 "models": {
  "ISRM": {
   "system_kind": "nonlinear",
   "expression_template_imports": [
    {
     "ref": "./isrm_base.esm"
    }
   ],
   "reference": {
    "url": "https://inmap.run/blog/2022/12/15/tutorial/",
    "notes": "Pure algebraic (no ODE state); every result is an observed."
   },
   "variables": {
    "W": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "shape": [
      "all_cells"
     ],
     "description": "Cell west edge (LCC m); from ISRM_Grid.W (full 596444, prefix used).",
     "update": {
      "kind": "data",
